[38;2;124;124;124mNow let me solve this.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe unilateral shift S on a separable Hilbert space H with orthonormal basis [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m{e_n}_{n≥0} is defined by S e_n = e_{n+1}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mI need to compute d(S, K(H)) = inf{||S - K|| : K compact}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key facts:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. S is an isometry: ||Sx|| = ||x|| for all x, so ||S|| = 1.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. The Calkin algebra: B(H)/K(H). The distance from an operator T to K(H) equals[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe norm of its image in the Calkin algebra (this is a standard result: d(T, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mK(H)) = ||π(T)|| where π: B(H) → B(H)/K(H) is the quotient map).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo d(S, K(H)) = ||π(S)|| in the Calkin algebra.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, what is the norm of the image of the unilateral shift in the Calkin [0m
[38;2;124;124;124malgebra?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe unilateral shift S has the property that S* S = I (it's an isometry), and S [0m[38;2;124;124;124mS* = I - P_0 where P_0 is the projection onto the first basis vector e_0 (rank [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1, hence compact).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo in the Calkin algebra:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π(S* S) = π(I) = 1 (the unit)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π(S S*) = π(I - P_0) = π(I) - π(P_0) = 1 - 0 = 1 (since P_0 is compact)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo π(S) is a unitary in the Calkin algebra! Both π(S)*π(S) = 1 and π(S)π(S)* = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore ||π(S)|| = 1 (since a unitary has norm 1).[0m

